Use make to build everything. Run tests by executing

   ./run-tests
   
You can generate data showing the mean and variance of an estimator type
of your choice by running

   ./generate-csv [type] [p]
   
Here, [type] is the name of the estimator in question (e.g. NaiveHyperLogLog)
and [p] the value of p used to choose m (m = 2^p). So, for exampe, to generate
data from HyperLogLog using m = 32, you'd call

   ./generate-csv HyperLogLog 5
   
This function outputs data to stdout; pipe or redirect it as appropriate to
process the raw CSV data.
